00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:42.120
The thing that really tipped
the scales for the vote.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:44.220
And it has to do with this confederation.

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:46.980
The most powerful, the
European Confederation.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.680
Specifically this guy, Michel Platini.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:52.680
A former French football
player turned FIFA guy.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:54.930
He was the president
of this confederation,

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:56.010
which inevitably meant

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:58.770
that he has sway over these other dudes.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:01.770
Just one week before the
vote, like crunch time,

00:22:01.770 --> 00:22:05.160
Platini got an invitation
that he couldn't refuse.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:08.310
A luncheon with the French
president at his palace.

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:10.110
Platini later said that
before this meeting,

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:12.060
he was planning on voting for the US

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:13.860
to host the World Cup in 2022.

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:16.860
But he goes to this luncheon
and who else is there?

00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:17.693
No big deal.

00:22:17.693 --> 00:22:20.490
Just these two guys, the
most powerful dudes in Qatar.

00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.470
One of them, the prime minister of Qatar

00:22:22.470 --> 00:22:25.380
and the other, the current Emir of Qatar

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:27.030
from like the old dynasty family.

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:29.430
It's important to
remember the context here.

00:22:29.430 --> 00:22:30.263
Like what's happening.

00:22:30.263 --> 00:22:31.410
This is 2010.

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:32.850
The world has just been rattled

00:22:32.850 --> 00:22:34.740
by a global financial meltdown

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:37.080
and the president of France, Sarkozy,

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:38.880
is stressed and he's in the room

00:22:38.880 --> 00:22:40.380
with the leaders of Qatar

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:43.020
who are not nearly in the
same financial trouble.

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:45.210
See the section before
about unlimited amounts

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:46.890
of money thanks to fossil fuels.

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:49.530
And it's clear that these
Qataris want something.

00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:53.010
Something that the Frenchmen
in the room can deliver them.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.920
A vote for their country
to host the World Cup.

00:22:55.920 --> 00:22:57.540
Something they really want.

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.580
According to sources
close to this meeting,

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:03.450
Sarkozy flat out told
Platini to vote for Qatar.

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:04.283
Why?

00:23:04.283 --> 00:23:06.120
Well, we'll never know.

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:09.330
But it's clear that he wanted
a few things from Qatar.

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:10.500
In this same meeting,

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:14.070
Sarkozy told the Qatari
that he wanted Qatar

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:16.920
to buy the French football
team Paris Saint-Germain,

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:19.590
which happens to be Sarkozy's
favorite football team.

00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:22.200
And at the time was in financial ruin.

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:24.810
After this meeting, a few
important things happened.

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:28.680
Number one, Qatar did end
up buying that football team

00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:31.800
for 60 million pounds
just like Sarkozy wanted.

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:34.950
They turned it around and soon
it became a star studded team

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:36.120
with merch that's worn

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:38.520
by the world's most popular celebrities.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:40.290
And then we suddenly see an uptick

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:43.410
in big trade deals
between Qatar and France.

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:46.860
Qatar Airways buys 50
giant planes from Airbus,

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:48.840
the giant French airplane maker.

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:50.760
I mean, if you look at what
one of these planes cost

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:53.400
in 2010, times it by 50,

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:55.830
we're looking at 18 billion dollars.

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:56.970
A massive deal.

00:23:56.970 --> 00:23:59.220
And in the end, Platini in this room

00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:02.670
with his president telling him
to do what the Qatari want.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:04.440
We need them right now.

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:05.273
And it worked.

00:24:05.273 --> 00:24:09.810
Michel Platini flipped his
vote from the USA to Qatar.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:10.800
He admitted it later.

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.360
That's not even speculation.

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.790
The president of the executive
committee, Sapp Blatter,

00:24:14.790 --> 00:24:16.260
was pissed about this

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.750
and later said that this
was the defining moment

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.610
for Qatar winning.

00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:23.790
- They have influenced Michel Platini

00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:27.120
at that time to vote for Qatar.

00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:29.400
- Because remember, Platini then went back

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:31.170
to his European Confederation

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.930
with eight executive committee
members, eight votes,

00:24:33.930 --> 00:24:36.570
and he almost certainly
influenced others to join him.

00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:40.230
One book I read claims that
he took four votes with him.

00:24:40.230 --> 00:24:41.430
But we'll never know.

00:24:41.430 --> 00:24:44.580
And then on a cold day
in December of 2010,

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:46.221
the day of the vote came.

00:24:46.221 --> 00:24:47.443
(dramatic music)

00:24:47.443 --> 00:24:50.070
- [Announcer] The 2022 FIFA World Cup.

00:24:50.070 --> 00:24:53.220
- [Harris] So on that faithful
day in the winter of 2010

00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:57.243
in Zurich, all the guests arrive
because it was voting day.

00:24:58.830 --> 00:25:00.390
- Every-

00:25:00.390 --> 00:25:03.390
- Clearly, I think we had
absolutely fantastic bid.

00:25:03.390 --> 00:25:05.520
- Well, we got a great bid,
so we just gotta go in there

00:25:05.520 --> 00:25:07.290
and give it everything that we've got.

00:25:07.290 --> 00:25:10.710
- These 22 men cast their
votes in multiple rounds

00:25:10.710 --> 00:25:12.960
until a majority victor emerged.

00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:16.470
At least 11 of them voted
from Qatar since round one.

00:25:16.470 --> 00:25:19.620
And finally, 14 votes
were delivered to Qatar,

00:25:19.620 --> 00:25:22.666
a majority and almost
double what the USA got.

00:25:22.666 --> 00:25:25.416
(dramatic music)

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:31.653
So yeah, that's how it went down.

00:25:33.030 --> 00:25:34.320
That's how it went down.

00:25:34.320 --> 00:25:36.540
Like, look, we'll never
know exactly what happened.

00:25:36.540 --> 00:25:38.910
A lot of this stuff we
know because it leaked out

00:25:38.910 --> 00:25:41.100
and we were able to put it all together.

00:25:41.100 --> 00:25:45.810
But the fact is every one of
these men has been involved

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:47.940
in some corruption investigation.

00:25:47.940 --> 00:25:50.640
I mean, it's no surprise
that this stuff happened

00:25:50.640 --> 00:25:52.440
and probably so much more.

00:25:52.440 --> 00:25:54.480
FIFA is corrupt to the core.

00:25:54.480 --> 00:25:56.130
Qatar didn't make this happen.

00:25:56.130 --> 00:25:59.940
Qatar just saw an organization
that spoke their language,

00:25:59.940 --> 00:26:02.040
the language of unlimited money,

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:04.800
and they used that to
get what they wanted.

00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:07.200
To prepare for the future, to diversify,

00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:08.850
to get the world to look at them.

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:13.523
- [Announcer] It is the
biggest event in the world.

00:26:14.580 --> 00:26:16.890
- So no, this isn't just a game.

00:26:16.890 --> 00:26:18.270
The reason why all of this matters is

00:26:18.270 --> 00:26:21.150
because football can be a beautiful thing.

00:26:21.150 --> 00:26:22.800
No matter what language someone speaks

00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:25.590
or their politics or
their God or whatever,

00:26:25.590 --> 00:26:28.500
they have this universal
language, this game.

00:26:28.500 --> 00:26:31.110
A global culture full of
screaming and cheering

00:26:31.110 --> 00:26:34.230
and crying and pride and identity.

00:26:34.230 --> 00:26:39.230
It's ridiculous, yet so
beautiful, so uniquely human.

00:26:39.570 --> 00:26:42.840
And in a very real way, football
is a mirror to the world.

00:26:42.840 --> 00:26:45.930
What's acceptable here in
this most revered sport

00:26:45.930 --> 00:26:48.270
is what's acceptable everywhere.

00:26:48.270 --> 00:26:50.790
So by using money and
influence to get the bid

00:26:50.790 --> 00:26:52.110
for the World Cup,

00:26:52.110 --> 00:26:55.770
Qatar showed us just how
power works in our world.

00:26:55.770 --> 00:26:59.040
They showed us who really
matters and who doesn't

00:26:59.040 --> 00:27:00.990
and validated an old idea

00:27:00.990 --> 00:27:03.750
that the rules of fair
play don't really matter

00:27:03.750 --> 00:27:05.500
if you have enough money.

00:27:05.500 --> 00:27:09.210
(slow melancholy music)

00:27:09.210 --> 00:27:10.290
Hey, thanks for watching

00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:12.270
and for sticking around
till the end of the video.

00:27:12.270 --> 00:27:14.550
This is just the first
of two videos we made

00:27:14.550 --> 00:27:15.540
on this topic.

00:27:15.540 --> 00:27:16.710
The next video publishes soon

00:27:16.710 --> 00:27:18.960
